module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.EpiLocallySurjective
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.WeaklyContractibleProducts
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ModuleTypesOnSite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentFromCoherence

/-!
# Local generation by finitely many sections gives Mathlib's finite type condition

Stacks 03DL(5), local generation by finitely many global sections, is recorded in this tree
twice: categorically, as `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite`, whose witness is a finite
coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf mapping onto the module; and as Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, whose witness is a family of generating global sections indexed
by a finite type.  The two are stated at different module universes.  The categorical form
takes its coproducts in `SheafOfModules.{max u v w}`, because `SheafOfModules.unit` lives at
the universe of the coefficient rings and a coproduct of copies of it must be compared with
the module after the universe lift `SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation`; Mathlib's form is
defined only when the module universe equals the ring universe `w`.

This file descends the first to the second.  The descent is possible because the universe lift
is an objectwise `ULift`: a finite coproduct of copies of the lifted structure sheaf mapping
onto the lifted module gives, after a choice of coordinates, finitely many honest global
sections of the module which generate it locally, and that is exactly the input of the
sectionwise finite type condition already in the tree.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_sections_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators`: a sheaf of modules
  generated by finitely many global sections in the sense of Stacks 03DE(5) admits finitely
  many global sections which generate it locally on sections.  This is the universe descent,
  and is the converse of `SheafOfModules.epi_powDesc`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_generates_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators_over`: the same
  conclusion for the restriction of a module to a slice, read on the ambient site as
  `PresheafOfModules.Generates`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite`: **the categorical form
  of Stacks 03DL(5) implies the sectionwise form `PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` on the
  underlying presheaf of modules**, at module universe equal to the ring universe and with no
  sheafification instance.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite`: **the categorical form of
  Stacks 03DL(5) implies Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`**, at module universe equal
  to the ring universe.

## Implementation notes

The coordinates of the finite coproduct are `SheafOfModules.powMk` and
`SheafOfModules.powMk_coord` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentFromCoherence`, and the chosen
generating sections are recovered from the coproduct's inclusions through
`SheafOfModules.liftSectionHom`, which is injective on sections because a morphism out of the
lifted structure sheaf is determined by the image of the unit section.  Comparing the given
coproduct with `SheafOfModules.liftPow` is the uniqueness of a colimit; no new structure is
introduced.

That an epimorphism is locally surjective is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.isLocallySurjective_of_epi`, which is stated at a
free module universe.  Its two sheafification hypotheses at the universe `max u v w` of the
coproducts hold on every site, by
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat`, so they appear in no
statement here; the only hypotheses carried are the sheafification instances at the universe
`w` which Mathlib's generating sections need on every slice.

The passage from the slice site to the ambient site uses `CategoryTheory.Sieve.overEquiv` in
the direction opposite to
`SheafOfModules.hasFiniteGlobalPresentation_over_of_generates`, and the generating sections of
a restriction are read on the ambient site at the terminal object of the slice, as in
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalOver`.

No `@[stacks 03DL]` attribute is carried: part (5) of that tag is already registered against
both predicates in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ModuleTypesOnSite`, and what is
proved here is the comparison of the two spellings, not a further part.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite SheafOfModules

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-- **The universe descent for Stacks 03DE(5).** A sheaf of modules admitting finitely many
generating global sections in the categorical sense of
`SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalGenerators` — a finite coproduct of copies of the universe
lifted structure sheaf mapping onto the universe lifted module — admits finitely many honest
global sections which generate it locally on sections.

This is the converse of `SheafOfModules.epi_powDesc`.  The given coproduct is identified with
`SheafOfModules.liftPow` by uniqueness of colimits, its inclusions are recognised as the
universe lifts of morphisms out of the structure sheaf, and the resulting epimorphism is read
on sections through `SheafOfModules.powMk_coord`. -/
theorem exists_sections_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators (N : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (h : N.HasFiniteGlobalGenerators) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (σ : Fin n → N.sections), ∀ (V : C) (x : N.val.obj (op V)),
      ∃ T : Sieve V, T ∈ J V ∧ ∀ ⦃B : C⦄ (g : B ⟶ V), T.arrows g →
        ∃ c : Fin n → R.obj.obj (op B),
          ∑ i, c i • (σ i).eval (op B) = N.val.map g.op x := by
  have hsh : HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v w} :=
    GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max u v w, v, u} J
  have hlb : J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u v w} :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max u v w, u, v} J
  obtain ⟨n, P, ι, ⟨hP⟩, π, hπ⟩ := h
  let e : liftPow R n ≅ P := (biproduct.isColimit _).coconePointUniqueUpToIso hP
  let q : liftPow R n ⟶ liftMod N := e.hom ≫ π
  let φ (i : Fin n) : liftUnit R ⟶ liftMod N := biproduct.ι (fun _ : Fin n => liftUnit R) i ≫ q
  let σ : Fin n → N.sections := fun i =>
    PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk
      (fun X => ((φ i).val.app X (liftUnitOf (1 : R.obj.obj X))).down)
      (fun {X Y} f => by
        have hnat := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (φ i).val f
          (liftUnitOf (1 : R.obj.obj X))
        have hone : (liftUnit R).val.map f (liftUnitOf (1 : R.obj.obj X))
            = liftUnitOf (1 : R.obj.obj Y) :=
          congrArg ULift.up (PresheafOfModules.unit_map_one R.obj f)
        rw [hone] at hnat
        exact congrArg ULift.down hnat.symm)
  have hqd : powDesc N σ = q := by
    refine biproduct.hom_ext' _ _ fun i => ?_
    have hi : biproduct.ι (fun _ : Fin n => liftUnit R) i ≫ powDesc N σ
        = liftSectionHom (σ i) := biproduct.ι_desc _ i
    rw [hi]
    ext X z
    rw [liftSectionHom_val_app_apply]
    have hz : (liftUnitVal z • liftUnitOf (1 : R.obj.obj X) : (liftUnit R).val.obj X) = z :=
      congrArg ULift.up (mul_one (liftUnitVal z))
    have hsm : (φ i).val.app X (liftUnitVal z • liftUnitOf (1 : R.obj.obj X))
        = liftUnitVal z • (φ i).val.app X (liftUnitOf (1 : R.obj.obj X)) :=
      map_smul ((φ i).val.app X).hom _ _
    have hup : (ULift.up (liftUnitVal z • (σ i).eval X) : (liftMod N).val.obj X)
        = liftUnitVal z • (φ i).val.app X (liftUnitOf (1 : R.obj.obj X)) := rfl
    rw [hup, ← hsm, hz]
  have hepi : Epi (powDesc N σ) := by
    rw [hqd]
    exact epi_comp e.hom π
  refine ⟨n, σ, fun V x => ⟨Presheaf.imageSieve ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj).map
      (powDesc N σ).val) (ULift.up x : (liftMod N).val.obj (op V)),
      (EpiMono.isLocallySurjective_of_epi (powDesc N σ)).imageSieve_mem _, ?_⟩⟩
  rintro B g ⟨t, ht⟩
  refine ⟨fun i =>
    liftUnitVal ((biproduct.π (fun _ : Fin n => liftUnit R) i).val.app (op B) t), ?_⟩
  have ht' : (powDesc N σ).val.app (op B) t = ULift.up (N.val.map g.op x) := ht
  rw [← powMk_coord n (op B) t, powDesc_val_app_powMk] at ht'
  exact congrArg ULift.down ht'

/-- Finitely many generating global sections of the restriction of a sheaf of modules to a
slice, read on the ambient site: they are finitely many sections over the object the slice is
taken at, generating the module in the sense of `PresheafOfModules.Generates`.

A global section of the restriction is evaluated at the terminal object of the slice, and the
covering sieves of the slice topology are the covering sieves of the ambient topology by
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff`. -/
theorem exists_generates_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators_over (M : SheafOfModules.{w} R) (Z : C)
    (h : (M.over Z).HasFiniteGlobalGenerators) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (s : Fin n → M.val.obj (op Z)), PresheafOfModules.Generates J M.val s := by
  obtain ⟨n, σ, hgen⟩ := exists_sections_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators (M.over Z) h
  refine ⟨n, fun i => (σ i).eval (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z))), fun W f t => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨T, hT, hc⟩ := hgen (Over.mk f) t
  refine ⟨Sieve.overEquiv (Over.mk f) T, (J.mem_over_iff T).mp hT, fun Y g hg => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hceq⟩ := hc (Over.homMk g : Over.mk (g ≫ f) ⟶ Over.mk f)
    ((Sieve.overEquiv_iff T g).mp hg)
  refine ⟨c, ?_⟩
  have hs (i : Fin n) : (σ i).eval (op (Over.mk (g ≫ f)))
      = M.val.restrictₛₗ (g ≫ f).op ((σ i).eval (op (Over.mk (𝟙 Z)))) :=
    ((σ i).property
      (Over.homMk (g ≫ f) (Category.comp_id _) : Over.mk (g ≫ f) ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 Z)).op).symm
  change ∑ i, c i • (σ i).eval (op (Over.mk (g ≫ f))) = M.val.restrictₛₗ g.op t at hceq
  simp only [hs] at hceq
  exact hceq

/-- **Stacks 03DL(5) in its categorical form implies the sectionwise one on the underlying
presheaf of modules.** On every object the module has a covering on whose members it is
generated by finitely many global sections; read on the ambient site by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_generates_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators_over`, those sections
generate sectionwise.

The covering family of `PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` is taken to be the objects of the site
which admit finitely many generating sections, which is why no choice of covering is recorded;
the given covering of an object refines the sieve of those objects.

No sheafification instance appears: the universe descent of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_sections_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators` manufactures the ones it
needs at the universe `max u v w` of the coproducts, and the sectionwise condition is stated
without sheafifying anything.  They are needed only to pass from here to Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, in
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite`. -/
theorem presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite (M : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (h : M.IsFiniteTypeOnSite) : PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType J M.val := by
  refine ⟨{Z : C // ∃ (n : ℕ) (s : Fin n → M.val.obj (op Z)),
      PresheafOfModules.Generates J M.val s}, Subtype.val, fun U => ?_, fun i => i.2⟩
  obtain ⟨I, V, f, hf, hgg⟩ := h.locally_finitelyGenerated U
  refine J.superset_covering (fun Y g hg => ?_) hf
  rw [Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff] at hg
  obtain ⟨i, a, rfl⟩ := hg
  rw [Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff]
  exact ⟨⟨V i, exists_generates_of_hasFiniteGlobalGenerators_over M (V i) (hgg i)⟩, ⟨a⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DL(5) in its categorical form implies Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`.** The sectionwise form on the underlying presheaf of modules is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite`, and that is Mathlib's
condition by `SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_presheaf_isFiniteType`. -/
theorem isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite (M : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    [∀ U : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : C, (J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (h : M.IsFiniteTypeOnSite) : M.IsFiniteType :=
  SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_presheaf_isFiniteType M
    (presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite M h)

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
